model g14_move_day_row
  tally 2
  on 9999-12-31
  start 9999-01-01
  end 9999-12-31
  note "T, tally 2.1.6 (#89, P7; #51), G14: L §7.6 item 1, §8.4: late's day is pay_day + 1 day, from a row's 9999-12-31, past 9999-12-31: load doesn't see it, so the instance is refused at its key (RUN-LIMIT), and a movement whose day is refused may fall on any day, so it refuses the places its legs give, konto and world, on every day (bal(konto) at 9999-03-31 too) and flows of late. The place spare, which only on_time touches, stands, and so do flows of on_time, dated by the row itself."

source plan "T's invented plan"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 9999-01-01..

place spare: accounts PLN lives 9999-01-01..

place world: outside lives 9999-01-01..

input pay_day: date

input amt: money PLN

move late: transfers
  on pay_day + 1 day
  leg cash from konto to world amount amt

move on_time: transfers
  on pay_day
  leg cash from world to spare amount amt

version plan_9999
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 9999-01-01
  pay_day = 9999-12-31
  amt = 15.00 PLN
  opening[konto] = 300.00 PLN at 9999-01-01 start
  opening[spare] = 100.00 PLN at 9999-01-01 start

ask k: bal(konto, 9999-03-31)

ask s: bal(spare, 9999-12-31)

ask f: flows(late, 9999), flows(on_time, 9999)
